From 3489a0a7b242e2006e7e2aec7d99198dd26f1e0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paolo Severini <paolosev@microsoft.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 19:46:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [wasm interpreter] Validate instance/trusted-data consistency

The interpreter selects an instance's interpreter object, handle,
runtime, module and signatures by loading the instance's trusted data.
Make the helper accessors re-establish that the loaded trusted data
still belongs to the instance before using it, so all interpreter entry
paths agree on the same invariant as the direct JS-to-interpreter entry.

Also tighten the per-instance indirect-call cache maintenance paths to
bounds-check the cache vectors unconditionally.

Add a mjsunit/sandbox regression test.

Also fix a build error caused by a change to the WasmDecoder constructor
signature.

Bug: 535518222
Change-Id: I11c52cdb365fd773fbc5e185f80dbcaad0231cf1
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8117710
Reviewed-by: Clemens Backes <clemensb@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Paolo Severini <paolosev@microsoft.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#108761}
